[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [{:db/id 17592186198443 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-2573d8ba-3c24-5f3f-9b87-70aaa707f60f"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-2573d8ba-3c24-5f3f-9b87-70aaa707f60f" :question/id #uuid "2573d8ba-3c24-5f3f-9b87-70aaa707f60f" :question/math-academy-id "q-170399" :question/problem "The maximum value of the quadratic form $Q(x)=2{x}_{1}^{2}-4{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-{x}_{2}^{2},$ when $‖x‖=1,$ is equal to $3.$ Which of the following is a vector $x$ at which the maximum is attained?" :question/worked-solution "Let $A$ be the matrix corresponding to our quadratic form. Recall that: \n\n- The maximum value of $Q(x),$ when $‖x‖=1,$ is equal to the largest eigenvalue of $A:$\n\n$$\nmax\\{Q(x)\\,|\\,‖x‖=1\\}={\\lambda }_{\\text{max}}\n$$\n\n \nThe maximum is attained on the corresponding unit eigenvector ${u}_{\\text{max}}.$\n\n- The minimum value of $Q(x),$ when $‖x‖=1,$ is equal to the smallest eigenvalue of $A:$\n\n$$\nmin\\{Q(x)\\,|\\,‖x‖=1\\}={\\lambda }_{\\text{min}}\n$$\n\n \nThe minimum is attained on the corresponding unit eigenvector ${u}_{\\text{min}}.$\n\nFirst, we write down the matrix of our quadratic form:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we need the unit eigenvector that corresponds to the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{\\text{max}}=3:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-3I & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}]-3[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $(A-3I)x=0$ gives the eigenvector $v=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$ \n\nFinally, dividing $v$ by its norm $‖v‖=\\sqrt{5},$ we get \n\n$$\n{u}_{\\text{max}}=\\frac{v}{‖v‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-80690941-9f30-50e8-8d51-0076ff14e552"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-80690941-9f30-50e8-8d51-0076ff14e552" :answer-field/id #uuid "80690941-9f30-50e8-8d51-0076ff14e552" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-835e0ac0-7f22-528a-afc9-15cbe76a1402" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e89e9894-f31f-51c2-beb8-dd440d12ff18" "answer-863bde5b-d22c-5fd4-9a26-b04e908b2888" "answer-835e0ac0-7f22-528a-afc9-15cbe76a1402" "answer-342b5faf-5467-5bea-910c-e959f5b08625" "answer-a2cffe23-ea90-5557-b734-2ff2fade4737"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e89e9894-f31f-51c2-beb8-dd440d12ff18" :answer/id #uuid "e89e9894-f31f-51c2-beb8-dd440d12ff18" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-863bde5b-d22c-5fd4-9a26-b04e908b2888" :answer/id #uuid "863bde5b-d22c-5fd4-9a26-b04e908b2888" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-835e0ac0-7f22-528a-afc9-15cbe76a1402" :answer/id #uuid "835e0ac0-7f22-528a-afc9-15cbe76a1402" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-342b5faf-5467-5bea-910c-e959f5b08625" :answer/id #uuid "342b5faf-5467-5bea-910c-e959f5b08625" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a2cffe23-ea90-5557-b734-2ff2fade4737" :answer/id #uuid "a2cffe23-ea90-5557-b734-2ff2fade4737" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-af4e152b-9159-5e39-89fa-52c6c18116b5" :activity/id #uuid "af4e152b-9159-5e39-89fa-52c6c18116b5" :activity/title "Constrained Optimization of Quadratic Forms: Determining Wh